Your words in your edition, and a search that finds what is already there
==========================================================================

Copy that was upstream's, now this edition's:

  "Personal workspace"  ->  "VolkDude's QuixiDesk"   (sidebar brand)
  "New task"            ->  "New instance"           (sidebar action)
  "Schedules"           ->  "Cron jobs"              (nav, page title, breadcrumb)

Naming a thing by what it is beats naming it by what it resembles: a schedule here is a command run on
a clock.

Tools & skills could only be searched half at a time — skills had a filter, connections did not, so
finding a tool you had already configured meant reading every card. There is now one search across
connections, the tools inside them, and skills, with a live count of matches. It re-applies through a
MutationObserver because both lists are drawn after the page renders.

